<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<component type="desktop-application">
    <id>com.selah.Selah</id>

    <name>Selah</name>
    <summary>A cross-platform Bible study app using Flutter and the 1769 King James Version</summary>

    <metadata_license>FSFAP</metadata_license>
    <project_license>Unlicense</project_license>

    <developer id="com.selah">
        <name>The Selah Project</name>
    </developer>

    <supports>
        <control>pointing</control>
        <control>keyboard</control>
        <control>touch</control>
    </supports>

    <description>
        <p>
            Selah is a touch-friendly Bible study application built with Flutter. It it designed to be simple, intuitive, and efficient
            by default while also offering a wide variety of features and customization options for power users. Some of the key features include:
        </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Customizable UI colors, fonts, and font size</li>
                <li>Word-level highlighting (with customizeable highlight colors)</li>
                <li>Support for verse-level, formatted notes</li>
                <li>The note system automatically generates click-able links for references</li>
                <li>Built-in support for displaying TSK references (Treasury of Scripture Knowledge)</li>
                <li>A simple search that also includes both advanced and unique features</li>
                <li>Seemless, transparent, account based online sync (no email required)</li>
                <li>Data exporting and importing to a portable JSON format (highlights, notes, verse history, and search history)</li>
            </ul>
        <p>
            The Selah Project arose out of the need for a high quality, preservation-focused, touch-friendly King James Bible study
            app for Linux platforms. But, because it is based on Flutter it also runs on every other platform without sacrificing
            any features (Windows, MacOS, Android, iOS, and web).
        </p>
        <p>
            The UI has been designed to support an efficient and pleasant workflow for **Bible-focused** study.
        </p>
        <p>
            Selah is still being actively developed and your corrections, feedback, and suggestions would be much appreciated, no matter
            how small. You can submit them on the GitHub issue tracker at <url>https://github.com/toazd/selah/issues</url>.
        </p>
    </description>

    <categories>
